## Verdict rationale

Functionally the feature works: state wires up, the modal opens via the button, the Link navigates to `/students`, demo branch is untouched, gating is correct, and the build is clean. However, the refined ticket explicitly specified `className="btn"` four times across requirements and acceptance criteria (lines 41-52, 76, 98), and `.btn` is a real shared utility in `app/globals.css:9` used by every other primary CTA in the app (`app/page.tsx`, `app/error.tsx`, `app/not-found.tsx`, `app/teacher/layout.tsx`). The build agent substituted ad-hoc inline Tailwind utilities — and used two different visual treatments for the two CTAs, producing a visibly mismatched header row. This is a documented spec deviation and a design-system regression. Per ruthless judging: explicit AC said `btn` class, implementation did not deliver `btn` class → FAIL.

## Notes for padi-eng

- Fix is one line per CTA: replace the long `className` strings on `app/teacher/grouping/page.tsx:221` and `:276` with `className="btn"`. Keep `disabled={!tenantId}` on the Add group button.
- Reverify visual consistency against `.btn` usage in `app/page.tsx:73` and `app/teacher/layout.tsx:47`.

